<title>GERMANY: German Deutz sells eco-technology unit.</title>
<headline>German Deutz sells eco-technology unit.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German motor-maker Deutz AG said on Monday it had sold its environmental technology unit to U.S.-based Baker Hughes Inc for an undisclosed amount.  </p>
<p>Deutz said in a statement the division had sales of around 160 million marks, and employed 350 staff in plants in Germany, Britain and the U.S.</p>
<p>The transaction is to take effect from July, assuming approval by German cartel authorities.</p>
<p>Deutz added that the U.S. oil services group intended to take on the employees affected by the deal and to continue to develop the division's activities.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 229 260 97 150</p>
</text>
